# 037-deepseek-responses-reasoning-text-echo.patch
#
# Vendored upstream PR #133799 (OPEN, DRAFT, author linfordWu, branch
# fix/deepseek-responses-reasoning-text) rebased onto v0.22.2, PLUS a fix to the PR's own
# gate that makes it a no-op on a relay host -- without that fix this patch changes nothing
# for this deployment. Upstream issue #133792 (OPEN, provider/deepseek, P2).
#
# Why: on the codex_responses wire Hermes persists and replays an encrypted reasoning blob
#   plus summary but never the thinking TEXT DeepSeek's /responses endpoint requires back:
#     * _capture_encrypted_item() stores only {type, encrypted_content, id, summary};
#       DeepSeek puts its thinking text in content[].reasoning_text (and summary: []), so the
#       text is discarded at capture.
#     * _preflight_encrypted() forwards only type/encrypted_content/summary, so even a
#       captured content[] is stripped on the way out.
#   Result: a mid-session continuation after enough tool-call turns is rejected with
#     HTTP 400: The `reasoning_text` in the thinking mode must be passed back to the API.
#   The error classifier files it as FailoverReason.format_error (retryable=False), so the
#   existing recovery ladder never fires and the turn dies.
#   The chat_completions wire already handles this requirement
#   (agent/message_sanitization.py _REASONING_ECHO_RULES pads a missing reasoning_content
#   with " "); the codex_responses path had no equivalent.
#
# After: _replay_reasoning_items/_chat_messages_to_responses_input take an opt-in
#   require_reasoning_text_echo flag; when set, each replayed reasoning item gets
#   content:[{type:"reasoning_text",text:" "}] and _preflight_encrypted preserves it. Callers
#   derive the flag from needs_reasoning_echo(provider, model, base_url).
#
# Deviation from the PR (MANDATORY -- the PR alone is inert here): the PR gates both call
#   sites on needs_reasoning_echo(None, None, base_url). That helper matches the must-echo
#   table on host OR model; DeepSeek's host entry is api.deepseek.com only and this
#   deployment reaches DeepSeek through the OpenCode Go relay (https://opencode.ai/zen/go/v1),
#   so with provider/model dropped the family never matches and the pad never engages.
#   Measured on the v0.22.2 tree: needs_reasoning_echo(None, None, relay_host) -> False,
#   needs_reasoning_echo("custom", "deepseek-v4.1-flash", relay_host) -> True.
#   Both call sites therefore pass provider + model (agent/codex_responses_adapter.py uses
#   requested_provider or provider, plus the effective wire model; agent/transports/codex.py
#   uses kwargs provider/model).
#
# Runtime files only: agent/codex_responses_adapter.py, agent/transports/codex.py
#
# Verified on a pristine v0.22.2 tree (d923a5eb):
#   (a) patch -p1 --dry-run -> rc=0, hunks land at v0.22.2 line numbers (offset +59/+60,
#       +43), no fuzz, no .rej/.orig; reverses cleanly (rc=0).
#   (b) py_compile clean; check_structure.py shows the +2 params and +1 helper region with
#       no class-body indentation change.
#   (c) Behaviour RED->GREEN through the REAL transport call path
#       (ResponsesApiTransport.convert_messages with provider=custom:opencode-codex,
#       model=deepseek-v4.1-flash, base_url=relay, one persisted reasoning blob):
#         pristine v0.22.2  -> replayed reasoning item has NO content  (RED)
#         patched           -> content=[{type:reasoning_text,text:" "}] (GREEN)
#       Control: with both gates reverted to the PR's (None, None, base_url) form the pad
#       disappears again -- proving the gate fix, not just the PR hunks, is what makes the
#       pad engage on this deployment.
#   (d) End-to-end against the real failing history (state.db session 20261015_203017_899c6016,
#       cutoff id 230890, 39 items / 8 reasoning items, deterministic triple-run):
#         BEFORE this patch: HTTP 400 "The `reasoning_text` in the thinking mode must be
#           passed back to the API." (request ids 056e5a41/3a22d83a/98ab83fe/60000a10)
#         WITH    this patch: HTTP 200 completed.
#       NOTE (recorded 2026-10-16): the relay stopped enforcing the requirement mid-morning --
#       the same pad-OFF history that 400'd deterministically now returns 200 (4/4 trials,
#       reused and fresh x-opencode-session, effort high/low/none). The requirement is
#       therefore conditional and server-side; this patch stays correct for the states where
#       it IS enforced, and is the reason the enforcement, when it returns, no longer kills
#       the turn.
#
# Retire when: upstream #133792 is closed AND the corresponding fix is an ancestor of the
#   pinned base tag (re-check with the ancestry rule, not the PR's state -- #133799 is still
#   OPEN/DRAFT as of 2026-10-16). Re-anchor anchors: _replay_reasoning_items signature,
#   _chat_messages_to_responses_input signature, _preflight_encrypted return dict,
#   ResponsesApiTransport.convert_messages, _native_responses_replay_items.
#
